{"id": "EUVD-2026-69232", "enisaUuid": "c3391771-3d63-31d7-b1da-ed89f8f7914f", "description": "httpd has never implemented obs-fold (RFC 2616 \u00a72.2 / RFC 7230 \u00a73.2.4 header continuation lines). Every CRLF followed by a non-CRLF octet unconditionally starts a new header. This missing feature became a security concern as the understanding of HTTP request smuggling attacks evolved.\n\nThis issue affects OTP from OTP\u00a017.0 before OTP\u00a027.3.4.17, from OTP\u00a028.0 before OTP\u00a028.5.0.6, and from OTP\u00a029.0 before OTP\u00a029.0.6, corresponding to inets from 5.10 before 9.3.2.7, from 9.4 before 9.6.2.3, and from 9.7 before 9.7.2. Whether OTP before OTP\u00a017.0, corresponding to inets before 5.10, is affected is unknown.", "datePublished": "2026-09-01T14:40:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-08T01:08:00", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/erlang/otp/security/advisories/GHSA-qh2f-33hj-37qf", "https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-66357.html", "https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-66357", "https://github.com/erlang/otp/commit/220d618d2479a7180b4a06d0c5aacfaa4af4a85b", "https://github.com/erlang/otp/commit/273d8958de38ff2a7fe0c5dcc5b6bfe6f65717f3", "https://github.com/erlang/otp/commit/e640d599287d2eba919e6f13b91f042d7dbe6ff4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-66357"], "assigner": "EEF", "epss": 0.58, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20ae590e-1112-3dfd-a3f9-fe54c4462316", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "9.7 <9.7.2"}, {"id": "5e608ae9-0c07-3c1d-a30f-187557615457", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "9.4 <9.6.2.3"}, {"id": "6b77191c-d9f2-3ed2-bfc4-2ab04db54c81", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang"}}, "product_version": "5.10 <9.3.2.7"}, {"id": "dc0b21bf-9ffe-3470-9ae1-b44487472bc6", "product": {"name": "otp", "vendor": {"name": "erlang